From 9232d6f4df08b128383f2c5f7e050c04989e780f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:13:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [DVBridge] Finish the GPU work of a frame that waits after
 its buffer swap

A frame of native Dolby Vision output presented the way that waits had its GPU work finished
(glFinish()) before eglSwapBuffers(), the order of the fork's first version. The commit that
follows has no in-fence: the kernel waits only for a fence that the driver attaches to the buffer
itself, which egl-gbm on NVIDIA may not, so what the swap has the GPU do with the buffer was not
waited for before the buffer was scanned out. Everything else already finishes after the swap: the
fence of a frame presented a frame ahead is made after it (it stands for what the swap does), the
frame without its fences after a refused commit (FinishDVBridgeRendering()) and the frame of the
GUI that goes out alone while a change of mode is held (FlipHeldGui()), whose comment says that a
frame of native output that waits does the same, which it did not.

Now the swap comes first, and the way that waits finishes the GPU work after it, in one place for a
frame meant to wait and for one that was meant to go a frame ahead and has no fence. Nothing else
changes: the GPU time is taken by its queries before the swap, as before.

A hardening: a frame scanned out before the swap's work has finished cannot be told from the
bytes that the check of the transport reads (it reads the GL buffer), only on the HDMI cable.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
index f1bc179..b2952ef 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -423,18 +423,20 @@ void CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::PresentRender(bool rendered, bool videoLayer)
       // (CHeldModeAnnouncement), which flushes the renderer: its GPU work is finished first
       if (m_modeAnnounce.Pending() == CHeldModeAnnouncement::Step::BEFORE_NEXT)
         ahead = false;
-      if (!ahead)
-        glFinish();
       const bool swapped = m_eglContext.TrySwapBuffers();
       // The fence is made after the swap, so that it also stands for what the swap itself has
       // the GPU do with the buffer.
       const bool fenced = ahead && swapped && DVAheadFence();
       if (ahead && !fenced)
-      {
         ahead = false;
-        if (swapped)
-          glFinish();
-      }
+      // Hades: the way that waits finishes the GPU work of the frame after the swap too, as the
+      // fence of a frame ahead stands for it, and as FinishDVBridgeRendering() and the frame of the
+      // GUI alone (FlipHeldGui()) do: the commit that follows has no in-fence, and the kernel would
+      // wait only for a fence that the driver attaches to the buffer itself, which egl-gbm on
+      // NVIDIA may not. (It finished the work before the swap, as the fork had it, and what the
+      // swap has the GPU do with the buffer was not waited for.)
+      if (!ahead && swapped)
+        glFinish();
       // Hades: the refresh with which the commit of the last picture kept on the screen in place
       // of a frame presented a frame ahead would have been flipped (KeepDVBridgeFrame()): waited
       // for here, as that flip would be. (Not the same as the flip of a frame, below: then there
